@@ -23,6 +23,20 @@
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Threshold Gating (Added)
+- `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` array: `[{ metric: "exact_match", min: 0.9 }]`.
+- Each threshold is evaluated against the metrics: score must be at least `min`, or the threshold fails.
+- Metrics with `score: null` (e.g., exact match without references) fail their threshold.
+- Report includes `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array of `{ metric, min, score, passed }`).
+- CLI `frai eval --threshold <metric>=<min>` (repeatable) parses and validates thresholds:
+  - Metric must exist in the evaluated set.
+  - Minimum must be a number in `[0, 1]`.
+  - Invalid thresholds exit 2 (usage error) with a list of valid metric ids.
+  - Threshold failure exits 1 (all others succeed); success exits 0.
+  - Report is written regardless of exit code.
+- Markdown reports include a "Thresholds" section with PASS/FAIL status per threshold.
+- JSON reports include top-level `passed` and `thresholds` fields when thresholds are supplied.
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
